    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 1.4 Visual Analysis\n",
        " Univariate Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "For continuous variables (Purchase):"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ySfKqlN_QXNU"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sns.histplot(df['Purchase'], kde=True)\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribution of Purchase Amounts\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "Tr08C9hnQbK6",
        "outputId": "8d77babf-b891-4d06-db64-3826d396117a"
      },
      "execution_count": 42,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Univariate Analysis — Purchase Amount\n",
        "\n",
        "Observation:\n",
        "\n",
        "Purchase amounts are right-skewed.\n",
        "\n",
        "Most customers spend between ₹5,000 – ₹12,000.\n",
        "\n",
        "A few customers spend as high as ₹24,000.\n",
        "\n",
        "Interpretation:\n",
        "\n",
        "High-value purchases are rare.\n",
        "\n",
        "Data shows multiple spending peaks (multimodal).\n",
        "\n",
        "A small segment of customers makes very large purchases.\n",
        "\n",
        "Business Insight:\n",
        "\n",
        "Walmart’s customer base is mostly medium spenders.\n",
        "\n",
        "Targeting premium customers (high spenders) can increase total revenue.\n",
        "\n",
        "Introduce exclusive offers or loyalty programs for big spenders."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cZPJSMdNQxa9"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# For categorical variables (Gender, Age, City_Category):"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3GeIdJK1Q7lO"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sns.countplot(x='Gender', data=df)\n",
        "sns.countplot(x='Age', data=df)\n",
        "sns.countplot(x='City_Category', data=df)\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 449
        },
        "id": "gWZNKAtTQ9R2",
        "outputId": "33b151ec-79be-4ffb-f3a0-72b1051233e3"
      },
      "execution_count": 43,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Bivariate Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "Purchase vs Gender / Age / Marital_Status:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qY6kU6OgRCog"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sns.boxplot(x='Gender', y='Purchase', data=df)\n",
        "sns.boxplot(x='Age', y='Purchase', data=df)\n",
        "sns.boxplot(x='Marital_Status', y='Purchase', data=df)\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 453
        },
        "id": "imFPEF3mRcWF",
        "outputId": "0b1b3183-3cb4-4446-e47a-a470b15d9b87"
      },
      "execution_count": 44,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Bivariate Analysis — Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "Male customers and the 26–35 age group show higher median purchase amounts, while married and unmarried customers spend almost the same on average.\n",
        "\n",
        "This indicates that gender and age influence spending behavior, but marital status has little or no effect on purchase amounts."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "kbx9Qk79SfEI"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#  Correlation (for numeric variables)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "C8xIM1GWRvRS"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "num = df.select_dtypes(include=['number'])\n",
        "sns.heatmap(num.corr(), annot=True, cmap='coolwarm')\n",
        "plt.title('Correlation Heatmap')\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 452
        },
        "id": "7cq5zGe4Rw1j",
        "outputId": "a1dac72d-660a-47d1-a275-5614937140e5"
      },
      "execution_count": 45,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Correlation Analysis — Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "Correlation values between Purchase and other numeric variables are very low (near 0).\n",
        "\n",
        "This means Occupation and Marital_Status have almost no linear relationship with spending.\n",
        "\n",
        "Customer demographics (like Gender, Age, City) likely influence purchase behavior more than numeric factors.\n",
        "\n",
        "Walmart should focus on demographic-based marketing, not occupation or marital status, for better targeting."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Lnb8KcinSQP-"
      }
    },
