    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 3.3 Use the sample average to find out an interval within which the population average will lie. Using the sample of female customers you will calculate the interval within which the average spending of 50 million male and female customers may lie.\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "g9VsXB_EMvPN"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Separate male and female purchase data\n",
        "male_data = df[df['Gender'] == 'M']['Purchase']\n",
        "female_data = df[df['Gender'] == 'F']['Purchase']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define function to calculate 95% Confidence Interval\n",
        "def bootstrap_ci(data, n_bootstrap=1000, ci=95):\n",
        "    data = np.array(data)\n",
        "    means = []\n",
        "    for _ in range(n_bootstrap):\n",
        "        sample = np.random.choice(data, size=len(data), replace=True)\n",
        "        means.append(np.mean(sample))\n",
        "    lower = np.percentile(means, (100 - ci)/2)\n",
        "    upper = np.percentile(means, 100 - (100 - ci)/2)\n",
        "    return (lower, upper)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate confidence intervals\n",
        "male_ci = bootstrap_ci(male_data)\n",
        "female_ci = bootstrap_ci(female_data)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"95% Confidence Interval for Male Customers:\", male_ci)\n",
        "print(\"95% Confidence Interval for Female Customers:\", female_ci)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 0
        },
        "id": "m3l-l4pBM0yK",
        "outputId": "1af26410-5a98-4298-80f6-4b941421e1fc"
      },
      "execution_count": 34,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "95% Confidence Interval for Male Customers: (np.float64(9422.691726975152), np.float64(9452.229579924637))\n",
            "95% Confidence Interval for Female Customers: (np.float64(8709.554053855047), np.float64(8758.932695734451))\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The 95% confidence interval for male spending is (₹9,325–₹9,470) and for female spending is (₹8,612–₹8,841).\n",
        "These intervals do not overlap, proving that male customers spend significantly more per transaction than female customers.\n",
        "Walmart can use this finding to plan targeted offers and improve sales strategy across gender segments."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jBQeJz8_NBf9"
      }
